Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:26:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] bsp -> 7f4693a: usb_retry in two steps, no main-loop
 stall without a USB host (felucca-bsp usb.c)

With no USB host attached (on battery, or a charger without data lines) usb_retry
ran usb_start in the main loop once a second: a 25 ms wait and six SIE timeouts,
29-41 ms in which keys, TRS MIDI and the screen waited. Now the reset and the
attach are two steps on separate passes, timed instead of waited, and a SIE that
does not answer costs one timeout. main_fm1.c calls usb_retry as before (the main
loop and safe mode's); boot, safe mode's start, the update loader's image and
everything while USB is up are unchanged.

In fm1-emu at 205 MHz, CYMA-1 1.1's play scenario: MIDI to sound p90 39.9 -> 7.4 ms
(64 notes), 0 xruns; a try 29-41 ms -> 0.5-1.8 ms of main loop. tests/run_tests.sh
passes (16 of 16). Not yet run on a device in this form.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
